        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Computes the transformation matrix <formula id="309">$ T_{\sigma} $</formula> to rotate a stress vector in Voigt notation into another Cartesian coordinate system. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This function builds the 6×6 transformation matrix from the direction cosines of the new basis:   <formula id="310">\[  \boldsymbol{\sigma}&apos;_{\text{voigt}} \;=\; T_{\sigma}\,\boldsymbol{\sigma}_{\text{voigt}},
\]</formula> which is equivalent to the tensor transformation   <formula id="311">\[  \boldsymbol{\sigma}&apos; \;=\; \boldsymbol{Q}\,\boldsymbol{\sigma}\,\boldsymbol{Q}^{T}.
\]</formula> <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>transformedCoordinateSystem</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>3×3 rotation matrix <formula id="308">$\boldsymbol{Q}$</formula> that maps from the original to the target Cartesian basis. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>6×6 transformation matrix <formula id="312">$T_{\sigma}$</formula> that transforms stress vectors in Voigt notation. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
